# Paths the `tauri dev` file watcher should not restart the app for.
#
# Gitignore syntax, relative to this directory (the one holding
# tauri.conf.json). The watcher's job is to rebuild and relaunch the Rust
# binary; anything it cannot change has no business waking it.
#
# The frontend is the big one. It lives inside this directory, so by default
# every file under it was watched — and a change to a `.tsx` file, or to a
# test that the app never imports, tore down the window and rebuilt the Rust
# app to show markup Vite had already hot-reloaded. Vite owns the frontend in
# dev; `beforeDevCommand` starts it once and it does not need restarting.
frontend/

# Generated and vendored: nothing here is a source change.
gen/
target/

# Prose and images. Editing a README should not cost a rebuild, and the
# icons are read at build time from the packaged copies.
README.md
*.md
icons/
